{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul","id":1185905,"title":"Questions about the Oneiros and the soul","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-14T05:35:54-08:00","id":1185905,"title":"Questions about the Oneiros and the soul","content":"1. Does the Oneiros of a person change after they're given someone else's soul? I remember reading that the Oneiros changes upon adopting a legacy or after creating a soul stone, so I can imagine their might be some kind of change, but my assumption is that they retain their original daimon, so the changes are probably subtle. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> 2. a. What happens to a person in the Oneiros of a person who has their soul severed? b. What if the person is in their own Oneiros when this happens? This seems like a question that is best answered at the time of the event, but I'm asking it in case there's already an established answer. My assumption is that either event would essentially act as a death in the Oneiros.<br /> <br /> 3. What happens if a person is in the Oneiros of a person when they awaken? Does the awakening abort? Is this a question best answered inside a particular game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6699-flux","name":"Flux","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T06:40:30-08:00","id":1185928,"title":"","content":"4. Is the Oneiros tied to the soul in such a way that possessing the soul allows access to the previous owner's Oneiros? Or is the Oneiros more a manifestion of the interaction of a sentient mind and a soul?<br /> <br /> 5. What happens if you destroy or consume all the Goetia in a person's Oneiros?<br /> <br /> 6. What are some potential ramafications of creating Irises/Portals between multiple people's Oneiroi? Hive mind? Mental communion?<br /> a. What happens if you Co-Locate multiple people's Oneiros (if that is even possible, due to scale)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T08:37:39-08:00","id":1185965,"title":"","content":"Every one of these seems like a question that could be an obsession, or at least be a mystery. Good stuff.<br /> <br /> 7. Can you get your daimon to become more powerful by consuming mana or essence?<br /> <br /> 8. Does your daimon even need essence?<br /> <br /> 9. What happens if you both swap daimons and swap souls? Anything different from just swapping daimons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T10:11:12-08:00","id":1185990,"title":"","content":"Being in a person's Oneiros shouldn't affect their Awakening directly, but it'll take you for one hell of a ride, since the Oneiros reshapes to reflect whatever the person is presently thinking about. If someone Awakens while you're in their Oneiros, that means it reflects the Supernal, pure and undiluted. So... If that happens, hold onto your butt.<br /> <br /> Also, if you destroy all the goetia in a person's Oneiros, it'll mess them up, but those things will eventually regrow. We've had examples from Dave of, say, destroying a person's arachnophobia, only to find it eventually takes shape again with time.<br /> <br /> If you summoned all the goetia out of their Oneiros, though, and bound them in a box, well... Suddenly that person is probably just a dull, emotionless husk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T20:13:33-08:00","id":1186166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1185928#post1185928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Is the Oneiros tied to the soul in such a way that possessing the soul allows access to the previous owner's Oneiros? Or is the Oneiros more a manifestion of the interaction of a sentient mind and a soul?<br /> <br /> 5. What happens if you destroy or consume all the Goetia in a person's Oneiros?<br /> <br /> 6. What are some potential ramafications of creating Irises/Portals between multiple people's Oneiroi? Hive mind? Mental communion?<br /> a. What happens if you Co-Locate multiple people's Oneiros (if that is even possible, due to scale)?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) a person might not even be aware his soul was stolen, the external factors from soul loss will probably manifest inside the oneiros though as they slowly spiral into a broken person.<br /> 2)again sleepers arnt probably even aware of soul loss, they just spiral down into thrall/broken territory and however that manifests in ones thoughts<br /> 3) Since being in an awake person oneiros is akin to viewing whatever they are doing at the time, its probably very bad to be inside one during an awakeing. It probably isnt going to stop one and you'll be lucky if you arnt dragged into something terrible while its happening. Best answered in each ST's game really.<br /> 4) no.<br /> 5) it will eventually reform, goetia get created for every astral scene so each time a scene changes inside an oneiros goetia are probably created or shifted about to act as window people...<br /> 6) you'll be able to travel via co-locate to the oneiros of whoever you have stacked? Space however works oddly in the astral as sympathy is odd there. (not sure how this translates to 2e though)<br /> 7) over feeding probably isnt the way goetia gain power, their strength is determined by other things (popularity, strength of gnosis for daimons etc) so i would say no.<br /> 8)Daimons probably dont need essence inside their own oneiros, they gain their rank every day in their home realms. They might bleed essence if outside your own oneiros, if you transplant one into another oneiros or even get it to the fallen world then it might start bleeding essence and probably reappear/reform back inside your oneiros if they hit hibernation.<br /> 9) soul swapping just reverses whatever stage of soul loss conditioning you are at, you can swap souls like swapping batteries in a watch. You dont get info (apart from excellent sympathetic links to former owners and whatever info those have) on previous owners of them or access to previous owners oneiros etc.<br /> <br /> Daimons are goetic astral guides, swapping them is probably temporary (i know daves actual play used this) but i think the original persons goetia would just reform eventually and (try to) eject foreigners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-14-2018, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T02:01:30-08:00","id":1186216,"title":"","content":"I agree with totalgit's post, but just a note on reformed Goetia: It's dream actors that are recreated each time the scene changes. Goetia that represent major parts of your psyche takes longer to reform (during which you lack whatever they represent in your personality). I'd use the rules for discorporated spirits to determine how long it takes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T05:11:53-08:00","id":1186250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1186166#post1186166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) a person might not even be aware his soul was stolen, the external factors from soul loss will probably manifest inside the oneiros though as they slowly spiral into a broken person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was unaware that you could enter the Oneiros of a person without a soul. I thought the Oneiros was tied specifically to the human soul. Assuming the soul and the Oneiros are tied together, the question was more asking how the exchange of a new soul for the old one would affect it.<br /> <br /> If a person can enter the Oneiros of a soulless person, that changes a lot of the assumptions I made with my questions. I'm seeing based on your answers that you believe that the Oneiros is accessible even if the human in question is without a soul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1185928#post1185928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. What are some potential ramafications of creating Irises/Portals between multiple people's Oneiroi? Hive mind? Mental communion?<br /> <b>a. What happens if you Co-Locate multiple people's Oneiros</b> (if that is even possible, due to scale)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this question. I don't have an answer, but it's a fun question.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6699-flux","name":"Flux","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T05:17:51-08:00","id":1186251,"title":"","content":"Since mages are able to work their magic (at least for a time) after suffering soul loss they still have their astral connection to their Watchtower. Part of that connection is the Oneiros, so while it might be crumbling and falling away if the soul loss continues, it doesn't instantly disappear along with the soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T05:36:24-08:00","id":1186254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1186251#post1186251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since mages are able to work their magic (at least for a time) after suffering soul loss they still have their astral connection to their Watchtower. Part of that connection is the Oneiros, so while it might be crumbling and falling away if the soul loss continues, it doesn't instantly disappear along with the soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was stated that those suffering Soul Loss have no Oneiros?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T06:07:23-08:00","id":1186269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1186254#post1186254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was stated that those suffering Soul Loss have no Oneiros?</div> </div> </div> </div>Their Onerios isn\u2019t gone, they\u2019re just not able to access the Astral at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T06:09:52-08:00","id":1186271,"title":"","content":"Ninja'd. Was just going to say that I'm pretty sure it's a connection to the Temenos that is lost with Soul Loss. Not sure if you could still poke around in your crumbling Oneiros or head out to the Anima Mundi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T06:09:57-08:00","id":1186272,"title":"","content":"Wait, I thought the Oneiros is literally your soul. Furnished and inhabited by your mind. So how does one \u2018enter\u2019 a house without walls, metaphorically speaking?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, so now I have this image of random furniture and suddenly homeless people being exposed to the elements as a metaphor for the foundation-less mindscape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 02-15-2018, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T06:15:09-08:00","id":1186277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1186272#post1186272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, I thought the Oneiros is literally your soul. Furnished and inhabited by your mind. So how does one \u2018enter\u2019 a house without walls, metaphorically speaking?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more like your house's foundation got ripped out from under it. You don't immediately lose all Integrity from getting your soul stolen (unless the spell has a whole ton of Reach dedicated to it) it just starts to crumble far more easily.<br /> <br /> The walls and furnishings are still there, mostly out of habit, because you're resolutely ignoring the sagging floor and the shattered foundations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T06:18:06-08:00","id":1186278,"title":"","content":"The core book states on p.98 that a soulless mage cannot enter the astral. My assumption is that this implies they lack the Oneiros to facilitate such a journey. My other assumption is that the ability of a mage to cast supernal magic is derived from their Gnosis which is supported by the soul. It\u2019s grip on the awakened soul is why Death 5 is necessary to sever it.<br /> <br /> Also, given that the Oneiros is called the personal soul, I don\u2019t think it\u2019s too far fetched to assume that it becomes inaccessible when a person is soulless. Unfortunately I\u2019m not confident enough to state any of this as fact, but I can illuminate my reasoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6699-flux","name":"Flux","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T06:23:05-08:00","id":1186281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flux</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1186278#post1186278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core book states on p.98 that a soulless mage cannot enter the astral. My assumption is that this implies they lack the Oneiros to facilitate such a journey. My other assumption is that the ability of a mage to cast supernal magic is derived from their Gnosis which is supported by the soul. It\u2019s grip on the awakened soul is why Death 5 is necessary to sever it.<br /> <br /> Also, given that the Oneiros is called the personal soul, I don\u2019t think it\u2019s too far fetched to assume that it becomes inaccessible when a person is soulless. Unfortunately I\u2019m not confident enough to state any of this as fact, but I can illuminate my reasoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this was my train of logic too. <br /> <br /> But then again, Arcanist made a fine metaphor up there...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T07:05:26-08:00","id":1186290,"title":"","content":"&lt;shrug&gt; I was thinking of working on a Reaper Legacy that stole souls, and then went on nightly (or more frequent) rampages through the victim's Oneiros, devouring Goetia for power or some such. Hence the direction of questions 4 &amp; 5 - to see if the idea is viable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T07:18:36-08:00","id":1186297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1186290#post1186290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;shrug&gt; I was thinking of working on a Reaper Legacy that stole souls, and then went on nightly (or more frequent) rampages through the victim's Oneiros, devouring Goetia for power or some such. Hence the direction of questions 4 &amp; 5 - to see if the idea is viable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, I love Legacies. <br /> <br /> Even if Oneiri and Goetia doesn\u2019t work that way, we can always say that the Legacy\u2019s Attainments specifically enable them to \u2018preserve\u2019 Oneiri and their Goetia so that it works that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T07:32:54-08:00","id":1186300,"title":"","content":"Considering some marks of a soul\u2019s former host remains in a soul after its removal (Legacy attainments for example), and if a soul is the Oneiros, it\u2019s probably possible to meditate into it via a dream bridge if you can somehow establish one. I imagine there\u2019s quite a jumble though, and when you pop it into a different host remnants start getting overwritten immediately by homeless goetis turning it into a suitable environment.<br /> <br /> Heck, maybe soul swaps are a microcosm of reality edits, pop a soul in and it\u2019s always been that guys soul, but there are random little details left over from the previous iteration of reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T07:41:27-08:00","id":1186303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1186297#post1186297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh, I love Legacies.<br /> <br /> Even if Oneiri and Goetia doesn\u2019t work that way, we can always say that the Legacy\u2019s Attainments specifically enable them to \u2018preserve\u2019 Oneiri and their Goetia so that it works that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>True... Hmm. I can see Death (Souls), Space (Remote connection), and Mind (Oneiros mindscape) being used, but legacies only use two Arcana... Off-topic here, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T07:45:15-08:00","id":1186305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1186300#post1186300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering some marks of a soul\u2019s former host remains in a soul after its removal (Legacy attainments for example), and if a soul is the Oneiros, it\u2019s probably possible to meditate into it via a dream bridge if you can somehow establish one. I imagine there\u2019s quite a jumble though, and when you pop it into a different host remnants start getting overwritten immediately by homeless goetis turning it into a suitable environment.<br /> <br /> Heck, maybe soul swaps are a microcosm of reality edits, pop a soul in and it\u2019s always been that guys soul, but there are random little details left over from the previous iteration of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder, then, if you could take a Soul Jar (containing a soul) into an Oneiros. So a soul in a soul. Extend, ad infinitum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T07:58:14-08:00","id":1186309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1185990#post1185990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B<br /> Also, if you destroy all the goetia in a person's Oneiros, it'll mess them up, but those things will eventually regrow. We've had examples from Dave of, say, destroying a person's arachnophobia, only to find it eventually takes shape again with time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You (or anyone) got this link? If I'm not mistaken, I thought Dave pointed out that you could destroy someones Goetia and get rid of the thought/feeling/memory/etc?<br /> <br /> But then again, if you actually can't get rid off anything permanently or make permanent changes inside your own Onerios, which I kinda thought was the whole raison d'etre more or less, why explore and do stuff in the Onerios at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T08:07:37-08:00","id":1186312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1186309#post1186309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You (or anyone) got this link? If I'm not mistaken, I thought Dave pointed out that you could destroy someones Goetia and get rid of the thought/feeling/memory/etc?<br /> <br /> But then again, if you actually can't get rid off anything permanently or make permanent changes inside your own Onerios, which I kinda thought was the whole raison d'etre more or less, why explore and do stuff in the Onerios at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>The key to getting rid of something permanently is to seal it away somewhere, not to destroy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T08:46:31-08:00","id":1186320,"title":"","content":"Seal it away or throw it into the Ocean Ouroboros. Or you can confront it, interact with it, alter your perceptions or context of it, etc.<br /> <br /> If I want to get rid of my arachnophobia, I need to wander to that nightmare realm and change its context. Break open the dark cavern; expose the nightmares to light; confront them and overcome your fear. That's how you deprive it of essence.<br /> <br /> The other way you can deal with it is, as Mrm said, bury the cave it's in. Seal it away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T19:04:18-08:00","id":1186516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1186305#post1186305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder, then, if you could take a Soul Jar (containing a soul) into an Oneiros. So a soul in a soul. Extend, ad infinitum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">\u201cSoul Jar\u201d is a unique case. Mages in Astral Space<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy-Italic\"><i>are </i><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">souls; they are treated as living bodies, but they<br /> are not. A mage can cast \u201cSoul Jar\u201d on a sealable<br /> container and, provided it is large enough, capture<br /> another mage\u2019s astral body in that container for the<br /> Duration of the spell.</span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>From 1e. Your astral body is (was in 1e the dream form might be the same in 2e) a soul but that doesnt make your onieros part of it.<br /> <br /> Not being able to enter the astral while soul less isnt the same as not having an oneiros while soul less. One presumes a mage with a soul could enter the soul less mages oneiros? At least thats how i see it, and cant find text to say otherwise so far apart from fluff text naming it personal soul, the soul realm etc.<br /> <br /> I just dont think that if you swap a soul the persons oneiros goes with it (since you dont get memories from a soul etc and the oneiros is memories etc). I can live with the oneiros not being able to be entered by anybody while soul less though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-15-2018, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T00:58:11-08:00","id":1186573,"title":"","content":"Does the Oneiros exist without a soul? I don't think it does. The clue to its nature is in the name personal soul. It's not called a human soul; it's called a personal soul. The Oneiros is created through the interaction between a human mind and its companion soul. (In the case of a Tremere, their not-soul probably plays a similar role.)<br /> <br /> I've been giving some thought as to why the human soul is special in the Chronicles of Darkness. The soul isn't unique in its ability to stabilize the mind or identity of a person. Both the Vampire's Beast and the Beast's Horror do this job adequately. It is unique in its ability to stabilize a mage's Gnosis, but that's an aside. What makes the soul unique is that it provides a blank canvas for the mind. It doesn't alter the identity it provides a substructure for unlike the Beast and the Horror. It allows you to be you, uncorrupted.<br /> <br /> So what changes to the Oneiros should we expect when a soul is swapped out? Probably nothing much. There may be some residue from the previous owner, but all in all, it should continue to play its role and allow you to be you.<br /> <br /> What happens to a person that is inside the Oneiros of a person whose soul has been severed? Since the Oneiros no longer exists, I'd assume they get punted back to their body instantly. They may or may not experience other consequences, but I think it's fair to assume they get back unharmed.<br /> <br /> This is what I'm comfortable with right now. It may not be what works for everyone else, but it makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> Of course, some additional questions arose from all this soul searching. What changes does a mage's soul go through that allows it to help reconstitute Gnosis better than a non-mage's soul? Does the mage's Gnosis itself change the nature of the soul? Is it permanent? Do Vampires and Beasts have something similar to an Oneiros where twisted Goetia dwell disconnected from the soul of humanity? These questions are probably best answered in particular chronicles, but I thought they were intriguing.<br /> <br /> Something else I find intriguing, souls provide a bridge to the Supernal (and the Abyss) and can only be interacted with via Supernal magic or by a Supernal being, and I also suspect that Abyssal beings are able to do the same thing. Now this is pure speculation, but I think it's possible that souls (human, humanity's, and the world's), the Supernal, and the Abyss are all spawned from the same super reality. Maybe it's where souls go when their owners die. Maybe this is the reality that all others sit on top of?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6699-flux","name":"Flux","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T01:36:08-08:00","id":1186581,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s actually not true that souls can only be interacted with by the Supernal or the Abyss, there are Numina for other ephemeral beings for instance that can snatch or devour souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T02:43:18-08:00","id":1186597,"title":"","content":"Ah, I thought I looked in the core book and didn\u2019t find any. What are the Numina that affect souls?<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, since new Numina can be created to manipulate souls and are explicitly called out as being able to affect souls, specifically named Numina in the core book or any other book is irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6699,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6699-flux","user":"Flux","date":". 02-16-2018, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6699-flux","name":"Flux","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T03:13:08-08:00","id":1186603,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and they\u2019re not the only things, though I can\u2019t remember anything specific at the moment. I think Second Sight has some soul stealing psychics or non-Supernal willworkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T03:46:55-08:00","id":1186606,"title":"","content":"Idigam has the power to pull the soul out of their victims and put spirits in the creating Claimed and Hive-Claimed. Strix also have a Dread Power for pulling out souls and putting them into objects that they can slowly feed from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T07:34:12-08:00","id":1186654,"title":"","content":"Didn\u2019t the Screaming Moon\u2019s Gift, an example alternate Moon Gift, have a power that ripped out souls? It\u2019s not published stuff, but I feel it should count. <br /> <br /> And let\u2019s not forget what fun the Unchained and their Soul Pacts bring to the table.<br /> <br /> Hmm... as I understood it, a Soul Pact doesn\u2019t actually claim the soul, but erases it and leaves a gaping hole where the demon slips in. This fits with explaining the soul as being what makes you You. When the demon claims your soul, \u201cyou\u201d become the demon. Damnation indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T08:29:46-08:00","id":1186674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1186654#post1186654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn\u2019t the Screaming Moon\u2019s Gift, an example alternate Moon Gift, have a power that ripped out souls? It\u2019s not published stuff, but I feel it should count.<br /> <br /> And let\u2019s not forget what fun the Unchained and their Soul Pacts bring to the table.<br /> <br /> Hmm... as I understood it, a Soul Pact doesn\u2019t actually claim the soul, but erases it and leaves a gaping hole where the demon slips in. This fits with explaining the soul as being what makes you You. When the demon claims your soul, \u201cyou\u201d become the demon. Damnation indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Additionally, Demons cannot enforce <i>any</i> Pacts with individuals that lack a soul. So it is obviously acting as the enabler for Cover element related shenanigans, regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T10:45:57-08:00","id":1186728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flux</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1186573#post1186573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Oneiros exist without a soul? I don't think it does. The clue to its nature is in the name personal soul. It's not called a human soul; it's called a personal soul. The Oneiros is created through the interaction between a human mind and its companion soul. (In the case of a Tremere, their not-soul probably plays a similar role.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Oneiros, like your mind, isn't your soul. Your soul is more like a rock on which a reef grows. If you made the reef disappear, all that stuff is still there, but it'll very quickly start to disintegrate. The Oneiros is made of your thoughts, your feelings, your Vice, your Virtue, your Gnosis, etc., all of which are draped upon the soul like coral around the rock. Remove the soul, the reef begins to collapse, but it's still there.<br /> <br /> It's necessary it works this way, too. Otherwise, there would be no Tremere; they initiate by delving into the Astral and wandering into the Ocean Ouroboros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T11:37:53-08:00","id":1187091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1186728#post1186728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's necessary it works this way, too. Otherwise, there would be no Tremere; they initiate by delving into the Astral and wandering into the Ocean Ouroboros.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is a good refutation of my conclusion. I could still be wrong, but this is 1e material, and it explicitly states that you can't enter the Astral Realms as a soulless mage in 2e. I'm less familiar with 1e material, so I don't know if you could enter the Astral Realms as a soulless mage in 1e or if the Tremere had a fix to allow them to circumvent the issue.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6699-flux","name":"Flux","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T11:40:53-08:00","id":1187092,"title":"","content":"You are correct; 2e is explicit that characters cannot enter the Astral without a soul. In that case, I don't know what to tell you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T00:36:17-07:00","id":1300485,"title":"","content":"*casts Deny The Reaper on this thread*<br /> <br /> So the Beast Player's Guide in Chapter 5 kinda heavily implies that Oneiros <i>are</i> souls. It specifically talks about &quot;enter[ing] individuals' personal soul&quot; (p151) and &quot;the realms of a singular person's soul&quot; (p154) in reference to the shifting qualities of an Oneiros as someone changes what they're thinking about and how they only really become stable when someone is in deep meditation. It also refers to Beasts as &quot;natives of the human soul&quot; and heavily implies that individual souls are sort of like roots or branches from the overall soul of humanity (which it implies is the Temenos, which I believe is pretty consistent with how Mage views the Temenos).*<br /> <br /> The implication then seems to be that someone who has no soul has no Oneiros.<br /> <br /> Additionally, given the qualities of the three soul loss Conditions in Mage, one could argue that the soul makes up the vital force of the mind (that supports its mental integrity - as represented by Integrity or Wisdom - and its will - as represented by WP) and both its connection to the larger entity of humanity as well as its capacity for sustaining higher consciousness (what with the loss of the utility of Gnosis when you hit Thrall).<br /> <br /> So it seems like the soul is the animating force of the mind, but not the mind itself - and that the Oneiros is the soul as it processes the mind it's attached to.<br /> <br /> The Nagaraja from Dark Eras also seem to lean in this direction as well - able to activate parts of a soul for the purpose of utilising active processes of the original owner's mind. This implies that while a soulless person doesn't have an Oneiros, the soul itself still is one.<br /> <br /> Additionally... I'm not sure that vampires don't have souls either - because &quot;the Beast&quot; is the antithesis of their Humanity (which is explicitly mechanically equivalent to Integrity and is affected by anything which affects Integrity), which implies some level of soul. Werewolves probably do too because Soulless Wolf is a thing. And Changelings can dreamwalk so presumably they have one also, albeit heavily eroded.<br /> <br /> *I kinda feel like this also answers why mages have not yet cracked how to make a soul - because they're not individual entities, and we're just viewing them like a 2D being would view a 3D being's fingers touching their plane of existence. So you can't make them because souls aren't made in the first place. It's like attempting to reshape the outside of an organism that you can only see from the inside, that also happens to contain a whole world, so that a little piece of it touches the measly fleshbag on your plane of existence. And that organism has an entirely ambiguous physical relationship with your plane of existence that you can only perceive by the parts of it that already connect to it. Welcome to recursive logic problems 101.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":1487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","user":"Zahaqiel","date":". 03-28-2019, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T00:55:04-07:00","id":1300490,"title":"","content":"Someone without a soul has no Oneiros.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t want to be inside the Oneiros of someone going through an Awakening. You don\u2019t get to see the Supernal, and the ride is... turbulent.<br /> <br /> Vampires do have souls, last I checked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T00:58:10-07:00","id":1300491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1186728#post1186728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Oneiros, like your mind, isn't your soul. Your soul is more like a rock on which a reef grows. If you made the reef disappear, all that stuff is still there, but it'll very quickly start to disintegrate. The Oneiros is made of your thoughts, your feelings, your Vice, your Virtue, your Gnosis, etc., all of which are draped upon the soul like coral around the rock. Remove the soul, the reef begins to collapse, but it's still there.<br /> <br /> It's necessary it works this way, too. Otherwise, there would be no Tremere; they initiate by delving into the Astral and wandering into the Ocean Ouroboros.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e was fuzzy about a lot of details like this. 2e Tremere have had their initiation tweaked to actually be possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T01:10:39-07:00","id":1300492,"title":"","content":"No Dave! Spoilers! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T12:53:08-07:00","id":1300915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1300490#post1300490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires do have souls, last I checked.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is news to me. I made the assumption based on what I knew of the Hollow Mekhet, the Jiang Shi, and the belief that becoming a vampire required dying. I assumed the soul flitted away to wherever souls go.<br /> <br /> Based on something you wrote elsewhere, vampires have a corrupted soul. This opens up questions of what kind of Oneiros they have. Maybe they don\u2019t have one? Same with Changelings. And Demons do something to souls too. Lots of fodder for speculation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6699-flux","name":"Flux","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T03:48:52-07:00","id":1301054,"title":"","content":"Demons (of the Descent variety) just outright burn off souls. They don't have them, they just consume/incorporate them. DtD has pretty explicit stuff about how powers that affect souls have nothing to work on when it comes to demons.<br /> <br /> But vampires have to have a soul for Hollow Mekhet to have their fractured souls. Plus there was an explicit discipline in 1e where vampires could remove souls from other vampires. Admittedly that one was a little weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T06:17:12-07:00","id":1301071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flux</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1300915#post1300915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on something you wrote elsewhere, vampires have a corrupted soul. This opens up questions of what kind of Oneiros they have. Maybe they don\u2019t have one? Same with Changelings. And Demons do something to souls too. Lots of fodder for speculation.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Beast, vampires have souls while changelings have altered/damaged souls. This means vampire souls aren't altered/damaged from being essentially human souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T09:29:02-07:00","id":1301083,"title":"","content":"Its's all really weird when it comes to vampires. The only time Vampire says that vampires have souls is in the diablerie section, but the effects of diablerie doesn't actually correspond to what's known about souls from Mage, and it's also explicitly written from the POV of vampires rather than being an objective take on it.<br /> Then vampires also die as part of the Embrace. In fact, the Embrace happens after the vampire-to-be has already died and the soul should've left the body. There's also Embraces that happen up to <i>a week</i> after the prospect has died.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-30-2019, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T10:41:33-07:00","id":1301096,"title":"","content":"A friend had a theory with the nature of the soul in the oWoD that may be able to be tinkered with to make it fit with CoD. You have 3 parts of the soul: Pathos, Shadow, and Avatar; also could be seen as Id, Ego, Super-Ego. The Avatar is what gives a person their mystical umph and most of the time stays asleep. When a mage awakens their Avatar allows them to cast magic and all three parts are basically equal. In a were-creature depending on which breed, the Avatar is an Avatar of Gaia and the shifting and gifts are the magic that the Avatar can use. When a person is embraced however, the curse forces the Avatar to awaken but also merges it with the Shadow as a gestalt, this new entity is the Beast. So a vampire has a soul but it can be seen as damaged or it can just be seen as altered depending on how the viewer interprets it. Maybe there is something there that can be used to describe the nature of the vampiric soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14195-kallarah","name":"Kallarah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T15:52:46-07:00","id":1301174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zahaqiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1301054#post1301054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons (of the Descent variety) just outright burn off souls. They don't have them, they just consume/incorporate them. DtD has pretty explicit stuff about how powers that affect souls have nothing to work on when it comes to demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mildly incorrect-their &quot;souls&quot; are their demonic selves.<br /> <br /> It amounts to the same thing, but when the academics need to slice lines, it's important to note that the Demonic Form is effectively the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T05:19:44-07:00","id":1301276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1301083#post1301083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its's all really weird when it comes to vampires. The only time Vampire says that vampires have souls is in the diablerie section, but the effects of diablerie doesn't actually correspond to what's known about souls from Mage, and it's also explicitly written from the POV of vampires rather than being an objective take on it.<br /> Then vampires also die as part of the Embrace. In fact, the Embrace happens after the vampire-to-be has already died and the soul should've left the body. There's also Embraces that happen up to <i>a week</i> after the prospect has died.</div> </div> </div> </div>So fun story on that.<br /> <br /> Demons have an Exploit called &quot;Raise Dead&quot;. It does what it says on the label, but has a caveat: if the person's soul has been destroyed, consumed <b>or has moved on to the next world</b>, no resurrection is possible unless you have a replacement soul. Additionally in both general CofD and Mage, souls are capable of existing independently of a body for a time - they're Twilight entities that are *not* made of ephemera, requiring soul-specific powers to operate on. So it's apparently not entirely unreasonable for post-mortem embraces to still work and create vampires with their soul - because apparently souls do stick around for a bit maybe. Going back to the Exploit &quot;Raise Dead&quot;, it is also affected by the passage of time, with it becoming more and more difficult to function the longer the person has been dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1301174#post1301174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mildly incorrect-their &quot;souls&quot; are their demonic selves.<br /> <br /> It amounts to the same thing, but when the academics need to slice lines, it's important to note that the Demonic Form is effectively the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. DtD is incredibly clear that demons don't have souls, they have multiple material states held in quantum superposition. You can't soul pact for another demon's demonic form, and a mage can't Sever the Awakened Soul to extract it. They also don't seem to be able to enter the Astral except for physically walking into it. So nothing &quot;soul-like&quot; really applies, it's a bit nonsense to try to force a comparison.<br /> <br /> Also souls aren't humans' &quot;true form&quot; either... mentally <i>or</i> physically. Demons don't have any points of intersection with what a soul is or does.<br /> <br /> In fact, the &quot;supernatural with no soul&quot; thing is almost certainly why Beasts automatically have an aura conflict with them when they break Spoofing - other supernatural entities are children of the Dark Mother, because they have some connection to the human soul. Demons are supernaturals that have never had souls and were never human, and are thus not in any way related to &quot;natural&quot; monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":1487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","user":"Zahaqiel","date":". 03-31-2019, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T08:55:37-07:00","id":1301322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zahaqiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1301276#post1301276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons don't have any points of intersection with what a soul is or does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the thrust of your post, but this particular part is, I believe, innacurate. If you look at <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/764484-what-do-souls-really-give-you\">what souls actually give you</a>, there are a couple points of intersection at the most fundamental levels, if not the more esoteric ones that you touched on in your post.<br /> <br /> Demons recover Willpower from Rest, and have normally-aligned Virtue and Vice, alongside not suffering from breaking points for indulging that Vice. This stuff doesn't necessarily mean they have a soul (it's fairly clear imo that they do not) but there is <i>some</i> intersection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T09:39:54-07:00","id":1301329,"title":"","content":"I can grant you Virtue/Vice, although Prometheans could also be said to be in the same boat on those despite also being kinda soulless (Elpis and Torment align to Virtue/Vice reasonably neatly). Creatures that have souls clearly go into psychological collapse when they don't have one, and Demons don't seem to ever risk that issue at all.<br /> <br /> As for the WP from rest issue... a lot of game line cores (and DtD seems to be one) don't actually explicitly state that - although I personally would presume that they do because WP calculations in DtD refer back to the CofD core, and it just seems like an oversight. On an interesting side-note, ephemerals also regain 1WP per day as well and several types can have Virtue and Vice.<br /> <br /> Basically, it seems like those are reality-baseline things for fully sentient entities... and maybe a soul is just required for human-branch entities to mentally function at all long-term... in which case it's not the soul per se that does it. But whatever does it requires the soul to be there to work for them.*<br /> <br /> 'Cause ghosts definitely don't need one for those things.<br /> <br /> *This may seem like a semantic dodge, but it wouldn't be the only thing that acts this way - Gnosis also clearly falls into this category of &quot;reliant on a soul, but isn't a trait of the soul&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":1487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","user":"Zahaqiel","date":". 03-31-2019, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T11:32:37-07:00","id":1301363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zahaqiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1301276#post1301276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it isn't. DtD is incredibly clear that demons don't have souls, they have multiple material states held in quantum superposition. You can't soul pact for another demon's demonic form, and a mage can't Sever the Awakened Soul to extract it. They also don't seem to be able to enter the Astral except for physically walking into it. So nothing &quot;soul-like&quot; really applies, it's a bit nonsense to try to force a comparison.<br /> <br /> Also souls aren't humans' &quot;true form&quot; either... mentally <i>or</i> physically. Demons don't have any points of intersection with what a soul is or does.<br /> <br /> In fact, the &quot;supernatural with no soul&quot; thing is almost certainly why Beasts automatically have an aura conflict with them when they break Spoofing - other supernatural entities are children of the Dark Mother, because they have some connection to the human soul. Demons are supernaturals that have never had souls and were never human, and are thus not in any way related to &quot;natural&quot; monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I don't care about how human souls manifest or interact in this conversation. Human souls are not the same thing as what angels(and to a lesser extent, spirits, goetia, and ghosts) are, and that's the basis of the core of understanding the &quot;demonic soul&quot;. By the way, those quotations are there for a reason.<br /> <br /> 2) DTD on the whole is pretty clear that they don't have <i>human</i> souls. What Demons are is essentially a coagulated angel wearing material states held in quantum superposition, ergo their demonic form is functionally, while not identically, the same thing as a soul for the demon. You can't soul pact or Sever the Awakened Soul on an angel, either.<br /> <br /> 3) Of course they aren't able to enter the Astral. The God-Machine is an invader to reality that has no grounds in any part of the Astral, and as such no demon is going to find themselves in there. That has no bearing that the effective soul of a demon is their demonic form.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying here is you missed the quotations and therefore massively missed the contextualization. The Demon's fundamental self as expressed in Demonic Form is functionally their soul, which is only of academic interest to most people because everything else here is true-it's not like you can do with a demon what you can do with anything else's soul. But for the academics, and also an understanding of What Primum Is and How It Works, it's an important distinction.<br /> <br /> THe Demonic Form is not a soul, it <i>functions</i> like one for the demon's personal purposes(and really funky occult principles most people won't even trip over).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:01:32-07:00","id":1301396,"title":"","content":"Humans don't have any natural ability for entering the Astral either (beyond, you know, just dreaming). Only a small subset of Sleepwalkers (in turn a small subset of humankind) can do that, and they should be much rarer, relatively speaking, than demons with Rip the Gates.<br /> There are two and a half splats that can naturally enter the Astral: mages and beasts, with werewolves sometimes having dreams set in the anima mundi in first edition. Also, it's the spirit half of werewolf that grants them that access, not their human side, and they end up at the part of the Astral that isn't derived from humanity. And now that I think about it beasts explicitly lacks souls, having their connection to the Astral forged by having a Goetia were the soul used to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-31-2019, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:06:38-07:00","id":1301420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1301396#post1301396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans don't have any natural ability for entering the Astral either (beyond, you know, just dreaming). Only a small subset of Sleepwalkers (in turn a small subset of humankind) can do that, and they should be much rarer, relatively speaking, than demons with Rip the Gates.<br /> There are two and a half splats that can naturally enter the Astral: mages and beasts, with werewolves sometimes having dreams set in the anima mundi in first edition. Also, it's the spirit half of werewolf that grants them that access, not their human side, and they end up at the part of the Astral that isn't derived from humanity. And now that I think about it beasts explicitly lacks souls, having their connection to the Astral forged by having a Goetia were the soul used to be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Beast: The Primordial does state that Mages can have their soul affecting magic work on a Beast with the similar requirements a Mage needs for affecting another Mage's soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:22:18-07:00","id":1301425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1301420#post1301420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast: The Primordial does state that Mages can have their soul affecting magic work on a Beast with the similar requirements a Mage needs for affecting another Mage's soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>It states that you can affect a Horror with magic on the same level you need to affect a soul. Combined with the whole soul-is-devoured-by-Horror it's really explicit beasts don't have actual souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:24:22-07:00","id":1301426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1301425#post1301425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It states that you can affect a Horror with magic on the same level you need to affect a soul. Combined with the whole soul-is-devoured-by-Horror it's really explicit beasts don't have actual souls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You mean besides all the times that the Beast: The Primordial book mixes up terms for &quot;Horror&quot; and &quot;Soul&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T22:09:37-07:00","id":1301512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1301363#post1301363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm saying here is you missed the quotations and therefore massively missed the contextualization. The Demon's fundamental self as expressed in Demonic Form is functionally their soul, [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>This part is the problem. Souls aren't a human's &quot;fundamental self&quot;. They have almost no meaning in the context of individual identity for humans, they're easily hot-swappable with almost no side-effects to the individual psyche of the receiving person. So academically speaking it's an incredibly forced metaphor that doesn't actually work.<br /> <br /> I get what you're saying - you're saying that a Demon's &quot;true identity&quot; is their demonic form. That is their &quot;true&quot; self. But that isn't what a soul is on any level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1301425#post1301425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It states that you can affect a Horror with magic on the same level you need to affect a soul. Combined with the whole soul-is-devoured-by-Horror it's really explicit beasts don't have actual souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also states that Beasts are &quot;natives of the human soul&quot;. Horrors are susceptible to the same things souls are, and they are creatures of the human soul.<br /> <br /> Additionally, in 2e, you're wrong about which splats can enter the Astral - Mages, Beasts, Werewolves (they can hunt in other peoples' dreams, which is explicitly the shallowest layer of the Astral) and Changelings (Gates of Ivory and Horn - they can both dreamwalk and physically enter the Astral).<br /> <br /> But more importantly, regular humans can too because there are Hunter merits for it that are available to any Hunter type (see: Tooth and Nail) and there are canonical human-run institutes that have researched Astral diving (such as The Merrick Institute, which experimented on regular children).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":1487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","user":"Zahaqiel","date":". 04-01-2019, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T22:36:01-07:00","id":1301519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zahaqiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1301512#post1301512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, in 2e, you're wrong about which splats can enter the Astral - Mages, Beasts, Werewolves (they can hunt in other peoples' dreams, which is explicitly the shallowest layer of the Astral) and Changelings (Gates of Ivory and Horn - they can both dreamwalk and physically enter the Astral).</div> </div> </div> </div>Talking of incredibly forced comparisons, this is one of them \u2014 &quot;dreams are the shallows of the Astral realms of the human soul&quot; does not make every form of dream-interaction Astral travel just because Dream Form stats apply (and werewolves don't even go to that extent, because equating &quot;a proprietary Gift of one subtype of werewolf uses the narrative background of dream-hunting to explain how they can remotely use its effects on a sleeping target who they are in the process of hunting&quot; to &quot;werewolves can hunt in people's dreams and therefore qualify as a whole splat that can enter the Astral&quot; is a reach).<br /> <br /> In the same section you're drawing this equivalence from, the Oneiros is called the lowest layer of the Astral <i>proper</i> \u2014 you may as well call people who can poke around in the ghostly Twilight surrounding a graveyard Underworld-divers if your criteria for being in another dimension is overlapping into someone else's glimpse of the front porch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T23:58:49-07:00","id":1301536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zahaqiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1301512#post1301512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This part is the problem. Souls aren't a human's &quot;fundamental self&quot;. They have almost no meaning in the context of individual identity for humans, they're easily hot-swappable with almost no side-effects to the individual psyche of the receiving person. So academically speaking it's an incredibly forced metaphor that doesn't actually work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you remember the coral reef?<br /> <br /> Well guess what?<br /> <br /> Your souls ain't a fucking shit without the demonic identity to claim them as part of themselves. Strip that away?<br /> <br /> It's like a coral reef without rock. Sure, you've got a ghost who remembers. How long that lasts?<br /> <br /> It's a fucking shit.<br /> <br /> Demons aren't susceptible to soul manipulation because they ain't got a soul. They ain't susceptible to it because all those fucks have <i>is</i> a soul.<br /> <br /> <i>This is not a contradiction.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-01-2019, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T03:54:33-07:00","id":1301569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zahaqiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1301512#post1301512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also states that Beasts are &quot;natives of the human soul&quot;. Horrors are susceptible to the same things souls are, and they are creatures of the human soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Natives of the Temenos. Doesn't make them souls just like it doesn't make any other Goetia souls. Otherwise your personal soul (Oneiros) would be filled to the brim with other souls (Goetia). Rather, the Horror takes the place of the Beast's soul, being able to be severed as if it was a soul, but not an actual soul unless we start defining souls by their function rather than what they actually are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zahaqiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1301512#post1301512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, in 2e, you're wrong about which splats can enter the Astral - Mages, Beasts, Werewolves (they can hunt in other peoples' dreams, which is explicitly the shallowest layer of the Astral) and Changelings (Gates of Ivory and Horn - they can both dreamwalk and physically enter the Astral).</div> </div> </div> </div>I <b>specifically</b> disqualified dreams. Neither example goes further than dreams. In fact, according to dev spoilers changelings would be closer to the Astral proper (the term used for all the realms beyond the Astral Barrier that separates dreams from the rest) while in the Hedge than in someone's dreams.<br /> Dreams would also qualify all creatures that do dream, including explicitly soulless animals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zahaqiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1301512#post1301512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But more importantly, regular humans can too because there are Hunter merits for it that are available to any Hunter type (see: Tooth and Nail) and there are canonical human-run institutes that have researched Astral diving (such as The Merrick Institute, which experimented on regular children).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter being on shaky cosmological grounds is no surprise to me. What works in Hunter doesn't necessarily work in other games. (Such as the whole lobotomy issue that Dave clarified.)<br /> Edit: Not that it matters. My point was that Astral diving is not a <i>natural</i> ability for humans. They need help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-01-2019, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T03:56:25-07:00","id":1301849,"title":"","content":"Werewolves can go into the astral, but it's not the Oneiros or Temenos. Instead when they dream deep enough for their minds to touch the astral (in the same way that rarely human minds can dream deep enough to reach the primordial dream), they find themselves in the Dreaming Earth in the Anima Mundi and they normally don't realize they're in the astral, they just think of it as a sacred vision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T06:24:38-07:00","id":1302534,"title":"","content":"The Oneiros *is* the personal soul, and is stated to be your soul many many times in both Mage 2e core and Astral Realms, so when you switch souls, you're almost certainly switching oneiroi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T14:32:35-07:00","id":1302929,"title":"","content":"This sounds like a question best investigated with outside assistance, namely from one of the <i>other</i> masters of astral navigation: a Beast. Have a Brood of beasts stroll into someone's Oneiros, mess with/destroy/imprison their Goetia in one of their Lairs, and maybe then transfer the soul with a Beast present inside the Oneiros...and just see what happens. Or have a Beast try to find and enter the soulless person's Oneiros after the fact by taking the long way through the Primordial Dream/Bright Dream (i.e. the Temenos). You could even have said Beast form a Chamber inside said Mage's Oneiros and see what happens when the soul is messed with. Play around, take notes, and see what happens. It'd be an interesting experiment for an academically-minded Beast with a Mastigos broodmate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/11.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":16101,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","user":"Eternal Darkness","date":". 04-05-2019, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16101-eternal-darkness","name":"Eternal Darkness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T14:54:29-07:00","id":1302936,"title":"","content":"Sounds extremely dangerous. The Oneiros might be a person's soul, but everything in it is based on that person's mind which is a whole different thing. Removing a soul means you separate an Oneiros from what it reflects. With nothing to reflect it will likely collapse, alongside anyone and anything within it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T18:22:22-07:00","id":1302978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1185905-questions-about-the-oneiros-and-the-soul?p=1302936#post1302936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds extremely dangerous. The Oneiros might be a person's soul, but everything in it is based on that person's mind which is a whole different thing. Removing a soul means you separate an Oneiros from what it reflects. With nothing to reflect it will likely collapse, alongside anyone and anything within it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless your ST uses reincarnation in their setting. I don't recollect the games *forbidding* it at least, and one of the fictions features a mage getting a new soul and being cautioned to watch out for weird side effects from the foreign soul.<br /> <br /> So I'd say that a soul without a host still has the goetia in it but it might maybe rot over time? If not certainly stagnate, or perhaps just calcify, like the goetia regressing to their most core concepts and features.<br /> <br /> So, I'd say it doesn't so much reflect the mind as grows and is fertilized BY the mind. Cut off that, and the ecosystem of the onieros will slowly change but I'd expect it to stay together for a time.<br /> <br /> But thats me, and Im the sort who likes the idea of even using onieros-delving to explore past lives. (obviously this is the scarier part of losing your soul in this case, losing your past lives.)<br /> <br /> as an aside, when I do this, all past lives have to be mortal or minor template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}